Heads up, Mara: two-way calendar sync (Google and Outlook) is already in progress under the Platform team. Leo owns it as PLT-212, with an ETA of Dec 4. A separate sprint on the same feature could duplicate that work or conflict with it. It may be worth syncing with Leo before Monday to decide whether Kai and Theo should join PLT-212 or take on something that complements it, such as the day-one onboarding experience.

Also, the production deploy freeze runs Nov 20 to Nov 27, which covers most of the second week of a 2-week sprint starting Monday. Only Sam-approved hotfixes can ship during that window, so nothing from this sprint could go live until after Nov 27.

